---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import FigurePlate from "../components/FigurePlate.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import { counts, formatCount, methodology, period, projectSummary, publicEventFields } from "../data/public";

const title = "FirePA — Methodology";
const clustering = methodology.workflow.find((item) => item.stage === "provisional_clustering");
const optical = methodology.workflow.find((item) => item.stage === "sentinel2_optical_followup");
const external = methodology.workflow.find((item) => item.stage === "external_reference_check");
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description="FirePA's frozen public methodology for provisional thermal events in Coclé, Panamá.">
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="main-content" class="docs-page">
    <section class="docs-hero">
      <div class="site-frame docs-hero__grid">
        <div data-reveal>
          <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span> METHOD / PUBLIC PACKAGE</p>
          <h1 class="docs-title">A reduction from <em>signal</em> to event.</h1>
          <p class="docs-standfirst">{projectSummary.definition}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="docs-hero__meta" data-reveal><p class="section-label">STUDY FRAME</p><p>{projectSummary.study_area}<br />{period.start} → {period.end} · {period.timezone}<br />Inclusive window · static package</p></div>
      </div>
      <nav class="site-frame docs-index" aria-label="Methodology sections">
        <a href="#method-study-title"><span>01</span>Study</a>
        <a href="#method-workflow-title"><span>02</span>Workflow</a>
        <a href="#method-rules-title"><span>03</span>Rules</a>
        <a href="#method-schema-title"><span>04</span>Public schema</a>
        <a href="#method-deferred-title"><span>05</span>Deferred</a>
      </nav>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="method-study-title">
      <div class="site-frame docs-section__grid" data-reveal>
        <div><p class="chapter-kicker"><span class="chapter-kicker__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span> 01 · STUDY</p><h2 id="method-study-title" class="docs-section-title">The unit is provisional.</h2></div>
        <div class="docs-copy"><p>The study covers {projectSummary.study_area} from {period.start} through {period.end} UTC, inclusive. FirePA starts with NASA FIRMS detections, audits the raw and processed counts, then groups detections into provisional thermal events.</p><p>The public package is frontend-agnostic and static. It does not require a backend, Earth Engine or network access to read the frozen records.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section docs-section--paper" aria-labelledby="method-workflow-title">
        <div class="site-frame" data-reveal>
        <div class="docs-section__heading"><p class="chapter-kicker"><span class="chapter-kicker__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span> 02 · WORKFLOW</p><h2 id="method-workflow-title" class="docs-section-title">Five passes, one public boundary.</h2></div>
        <ol class="method-steps">
          {methodology.workflow.map((item, index) => (
            <li class="method-step">
              <span class="method-step__number">0{index + 1}</span>
              <div><h3>{item.stage.replaceAll("_", " ")}</h3><p>{item.result}</p><p class="method-step__meta"><code>{item.status}</code>{item.configuration_id && <><span>·</span><code>{item.configuration_id}</code></>}{item.algorithm && <><span>·</span><code>{item.algorithm}</code></>}</p></div>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="method-rules-title">
      <div class="site-frame docs-section__grid" data-reveal>
        <div><p class="chapter-kicker"><span class="chapter-kicker__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span> 03 · RULES</p><h2 id="method-rules-title" class="docs-section-title">Keep the rule visible.</h2></div>
        <div class="docs-copy docs-copy--facts">
          <dl class="docs-facts">
            <div><dt>Clustering</dt><dd>{clustering?.radius_m} m radius · {clustering?.time_window_hours} h window · {clustering?.metric_projection}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Algorithm</dt><dd>{clustering?.algorithm} · {counts.configuration_id}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Optical cohort</dt><dd>{optical?.cohort_events} cases · {optical?.observable_events} observable · {optical?.unobserved_events} unobserved</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Evidence modes</dt><dd>{optical?.evidence_modes?.join(" / ")}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>NBR / dNBR</dt><dd>Descriptive metrics only; no severity class.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>External check</dt><dd>{external?.matching_rule} · reclustered: {String(external?.reclustered)}</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p>{external?.result} The two public references are relational checks, not ground truth.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section docs-section--dark" aria-labelledby="method-schema-title">
      <div class="site-frame docs-section__grid" data-reveal>
        <div><p class="chapter-kicker"><span class="chapter-kicker__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span> 04 · PUBLIC SCHEMA</p><h2 id="method-schema-title" class="docs-section-title">Nineteen fields, no hidden row.</h2></div>
        <div class="docs-copy"><p>The public event explorer exposes the fields below. Coordinates are public WGS84 centroids. The schema does not publish raw detection rows, scene paths, private IDs or reviewer identities.</p><div class="schema-list">{publicEventFields.map((field) => <code>{field}</code>)}</div></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="method-deferred-title">
      <div class="site-frame docs-section__grid" data-reveal>
        <div><p class="chapter-kicker"><span class="chapter-kicker__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span> 05 · DEFERRED</p><h2 id="method-deferred-title" class="docs-section-title">What this release does not add.</h2></div>
        <div class="docs-copy"><p>Formal human review remains deferred: {methodology.formal_review.reason}. The public count of formal observations is {methodology.formal_review.formal_human_observations}. Supervised modeling remains deferred: {methodology.supervised_modeling.reason}.</p><p>Those are evidence boundaries, not empty interface states. See <a class="text-link" href="/sources">Sources &amp; provenance ↗</a> for the frozen references and hashes.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="site-frame docs-figure-band" data-reveal>
      <FigurePlate
        figureId="figure-01"
        src="/figures/01_pipeline_overview.png"
        alt="Frozen FirePA pipeline overview from FIRMS detections through provisional events and the optical follow-up."
        title="The frozen pipeline"
        caption={`The public package counts ${formatCount(counts.firms_raw_detections)} raw detections, ${formatCount(counts.firms_processed_detections)} processed detections and ${formatCount(counts.provisional_thermal_events)} provisional events before the optical follow-up.`}
        longDescription="The frozen pipeline overview records the audited FIRMS counts, the r1500_t06 clustering configuration, the 611 provisional events, the 30-event Sentinel-2 pilot, the two external reference checks and the public release boundary."
      />
    </div>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
